  "schema": "trial/1",
  "trial": "P-73",
  "question": "What does the Checks API take of one neutral check run's annotations: how many in one request, how many in all over updates, the longest message kept whole, and does it keep an annotation on a path outside the pull request's diff, or one with no line?",
  "pass": "Written before the run, in issue 1030 at 2026-11-20T18:18Z, nothing having run (trial TA4 of decision 0224's plan): in the canary, on a pull request of the trial's own that changes p73/a.py (canary pull request 132, branch trial/p-73, head 410baec), a workflow with its own GITHUB_TOKEN, granted checks write, makes completed neutral check runs: 1, 50 and 51 annotations; three updates of 50 more to the run of 50, then its annotations listed; a message of 65,536 and of 65,535 ASCII characters, each read back; an annotation on README.md, which the change does not touch; one with no start_line or end_line. The writer is GitHub Actions' App, not the Factory's: the annotation limits are the Checks API's, the same for every App, and this session may not mint the Factory App's token. Each answer was written to a file in the job and redacted there by software-factory's tools.redact_trial at d53baceb before it was uploaded. Pass: each is answered by what GitHub returned and recorded; it fails only if an answer cannot be read. Result, of what this file's own exchanges hold: one request takes 1 annotation, 201; one of 51 is refused, 422, 'No more than 50 items are allowed; 51 were supplied.', giving no run; the third page of the run of 50's annotations holds none; one with no start_line and end_line is refused, 422, '\"end_line\", \"start_line\" weren't supplied.'; read again by the Maintainer under a minute after the run, the run of 50 holds 150, so a run holds at least 150 and no limit was met, and the annotation on README.md, which the change does not touch, is listed. The Factory's own limits (adapters/advice.py: 50 in one request, a message of at most 8,000 characters) sit within each; a Finding with no line cannot be an annotation. Passed. What this file keeps (2026-11-21, to fit the review's size bound): exchanges 0, 2, 8, 15, 16 and 17 of the trial's 18, in the order they happened. Owed in P-73.messages.json: the message of 65,536 ASCII characters taken, 201, and kept cut to 65,535 with no word of it, the one of 65,535 kept whole, the annotation off the diff created, and its list asked about two seconds after its create answering 404. Owed in P-73.fifty.json: the create of the run of 50 and its first update, which took it to 100. Owed in P-73.updates.json: the second update, sent in the same second as the first's 200, answering 404 and not asked again, so its 50 are not among those listed, and the third, which took the run to 150. The first two pages of the run's annotations, of 100 and 50, are not kept: their counts and sha256 are in the call of the last read after the run, exchange 5 here.",
